{
  "case": "cn-n-reference-region-multi-process",
  "clause": "DESIGN R3.3 §7.2 Reference region, Relation direction, Structure; §4.4 sharing; §7.3 multi-process/shared references",
  "author": "spec-seal",
  "operation": "normalize",
  "profile": "cn-n",
  "derivation": "One root DataStore shared by two Processes, one DataStoreReference per Process: each Process gets its own Collaboration and main Participant (ensure-base-supports) and, because references need it, its own reference band; the second ensure of each Collaboration in ensure-reference-band is an identical plan and coalesces (reported once, under the first recipe). Link_B (Task -> reference) is the unambiguous reversed pair: ids preserved, endpoints swapped, direction One. Each reference is placed in region reference of its own Process with its own link; the store is neither duplicated nor placed.",
